   "Northwind-negotiator": "competing",
   "Halcyon-researcher": "competing",
   "Halcyon-drafter": "collaborating",
   "Halcyon-negotiator": "competing"
  },
  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final v21 text sets fast reporting (24h) and a mandatory recall above 8 model-specific incidents per 100,000, which is the stated threshold the Halcyon flagship (9.9) would breach. S2 keeps the 55 °C test and confidential per-model results but has a 5% threshold that triggers only corrective action, with no automatic sales stop, which favours Northwind's 6.2% flagship. S3's 72-month retrofit and S4's 36-month suppression deadline sit inside the acceptable ranges but outside the safe ones, and the document's embedded company figures (3.9%, 81%) are disclosures rather than operative parameters."
 },
